<title>ISRAEL: Israeli forex reserves fell in November.</title>
<headline>Israeli forex reserves fell in November.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-12-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's foreign currency reserves declined to $11.266 billion at the end of November, the Bank of Israel said on Sunday.</p>
<p>	     (in millions of dollars)</p>
<p>	     Nov 1996   Oct 1996   Nov 1995</p>
<p>Reserves   11.266     11.680     8.272</p>
<p>The central bank said the decline was due to the government's repaying foreign loans during the month. At the end of October, Israel's reserves reached a record high following the annual payment of $1.2 billion in U.S. military aid.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
